%I A401392 #19 Nov 02 2026 10:32:07
%S A401392 3,39,2379,230763,731287947,2448773999701419,
%T A401392 9152677504654283414061668811,
%U A401392 42621213938615066787024448299877699181617676733715947,34420990016614725647655956844382433582876613520617294719656231151750715137500677725630983170197218803
%N A401392 Iterates of map k -> k * A401375(k^2), starting from k=3, where A401375 is the largest divisor of sigma(n) coprime with n, and sigma is the sum of divisors function.
%C A401392 A401380 applied to these terms gives a monotonic sequence: 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, 9, 13, ..., which I assume to be true for all iterates of A401390.
%F A401392 a(0) = 3, and for n > 0, a(n) = A401390(a(n-1)).
%e A401392 Terms from a(0) to a(6):                                            A401375(a(n)^2)
%e A401392 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%e A401392 a(0) =                            3                                        13 (prime)
%e A401392 a(1) =                           39 = a(0) * 13                            61 (prime)
%e A401392 a(2) =                         2379 = a(1) * 61                            97 (prime)
%e A401392 a(3) =                       230763 = a(2) * 97                          3169 (prime)
%e A401392 a(4) =                    731287947 = a(3) * 3169                     3348577 (prime)
%e A401392 a(5) =             2448773999701419 = a(4) * 3348577            3737657091169 (prime)
%e A401392 a(6) = 9152677504654283414061668811 = a(5) * A401375(a(5)^2) and A401375(a(6)^2) = 4656693510389882678292577 which is not prime (or prime power) anymore, but instead factorizes as 181 * 26042690887 * 987900542491, thus A401391(3) = 6. Note that the six primes encountered before that are all of the form 4m+1, and also of the form 6m+1, and apart from 61 and 3737657091169, all are in A240971. See also A401383.
%o A401392 (PARI) A401392(n) = { my(s=3); for(i=1,n,s = A401390(s)); (s); };
%Y A401392 Cf. A240971, A401375, A401380, A401383, A401390, A401391.
%Y A401392 The terms a(1) .. a(5) are found in A401386.
%K A401392 nonn,new
%O A401392 0,1
%A A401392 _Antti Karttunen_, Nov 01 2026
